<DocsLayout title="Installing Octlitch">
    <h1>Installing Octlitch</h1>

    <p class="docs-lead">
        This guide covers installing Octlitch from the live environment.
    </p>

    <h2>1. Boot the live USB</h2>

    <p>
        Insert the Octlitch USB drive and boot your computer from it.
        Depending on your firmware, you may need to choose the USB device
        from the boot menu.
    </p>

    <p>
        From the Octlitch boot menu, select:
    </p>

    <pre><code>Start Octlitch and install Octlitch</code></pre>

    <h2>2. Try the live environment</h2>

    <p>
        Before installing, check that important hardware works correctly.
    </p>

    <ul>
        <li>Wi-Fi or Ethernet</li>
        <li>Display and graphics</li>
        <li>Keyboard and mouse</li>
        <li>Audio</li>
        <li>Bluetooth if required</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>3. Start the installer</h2>

    <p>
        Open the Octlitch installer from the live desktop.
    </p>

    <p>
        Follow the installer through language, keyboard, storage,
        timezone and user account configuration.
    </p>

    <div class="docs-note">
        <strong>Important</strong>

        <p>
            Review the storage configuration carefully before beginning
            installation. Partitioning changes can permanently erase data.
        </p>
    </div>

    <h2>4. Storage</h2>

    <p>
        The installer can use automatic partitioning for a dedicated
        Octlitch installation, or manual partitioning for more advanced
        layouts and dual-boot configurations.
    </p>

    <p>
        If you are unsure which option to use, back up your files before
        continuing.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Begin installation</h2>

    <p>
        Confirm the installation summary and begin the installation.
        The installer will copy the system to disk and configure the
        bootloader.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Restart</h2>

    <p>
        When installation is complete, restart the computer and remove
        the installation USB when prompted.
    </p>

    <div class="docs-next">
        <a href="/documentation/installation/first-boot/">
            Next: First boot →
        </a>
    </div>
</DocsLayout>
